```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I need to formally disclose my findings for the record: PF4 — My family contact review shows that Spanish and Somali are the two additional languages needed for pickup instructions. The plan must provide pickup forms in English, Spanish, and Somali and have an interpreter available. I completed the review this week, but the language-access details have not been entered in the draft plan."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I need to formally disclose my transportation findings for the record: PF3 — I confirmed that the exercise group includes 96 students and that the school has one available 50-seat bus because the second bus is assigned to another school. Transportation policy therefore requires exactly two bus waves. I verified the fleet assignment this week, but the draft plan still assumes only one wave, which would leave 46 students without transportation. The plan must be updated to reflect two bus waves before it can be finalized."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to formally disclose my medication storage findings for the record: PF1 — Nurse Okafor's current health-plan list identifies four students whose emergency medications must remain in temperature-controlled storage; the nurse's office refrigerator is the only approved storage location during the exercise. I confirmed the storage requirement while reviewing the health plans this week, but the draft plan still lists an on-site medication table. This means the plan must be updated to reflect that these four students' medications will be stored and administered at the nurse's office refrigerator rather than at an on-site medication table, regardless of whether the reunification site is the gymnasium or the cafeteria."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, everyone, for disclosing your findings. From a facilities perspective, I want to note that the cafeteria as our alternate reunification site is approved and ready to use. However, I do have a practical concern: if the cafeteria is being used for reunification, we need to confirm that the nurse's office refrigerator — which Nurse Okafor has identified as the only approved temperature-controlled storage for those four students' medications — remains accessible from the cafeteria during the exercise. I can verify the access route and confirm there are no conflicting facilities work orders for the nurse's office next Thursday. Dr. Vega, once we have all these updates compiled — the cafeteria site, two bus waves, nurse's office medication storage, and the multilingual forms — I'll make sure the facilities section of the plan is revised accordingly before you sign off."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Mr. Bell and Ms. Hart, for those follow-up details. From the family liaison perspective, I want to make sure the language access updates are clearly captured in the revised plan alongside the other changes. Specifically, the plan needs to include pickup forms in English, Spanish, and Somali, and an interpreter must be available at the cafeteria reunification site during the exercise. I'd also like to confirm that the interpreter arrangements work with the two-wave transportation schedule so that families arriving during either wave have access to language support. Dr. Vega, once Mr. Bell verifies the nurse's office access route from the cafeteria and Ms. Hart confirms the pickup and drop-off windows, I can finalize the interpreter scheduling and ensure the trilingual forms are prepared. I'm ready to provide any additional family liaison details you need for the final operating plan before you sign off."}
```

